title: dictionaryValue has no implicit conversion to uint64
updated_at: "2026-09-08T21:46:03Z"
---
## Goal
Flag implicit conversion from `dictionaryValue` to `uint64`. Game typedb exposes `int64 opConv()` and `double opConv()` only — not `uint64`.

## Source
tm-editor-plus-plus `src/Dev/FindPatternCached.as` (2026-09-02). Game compile failed; `openplanet-lsp check` reported 0 errors (24 unrelated warnings).

## Repro
```angelscript
dictionary _cache;
uint64 Get(const string &in pat) {
    if (_cache.Exists(pat)) {
        return _cache[pat];
    }
    return 0;
}
```

## Compiler (game-side)
```
Dev/FindPatternCached.as (6, 13) :  ERR : No conversion from 'dictionaryValue' to 'uint64' available.
```

## LSP today
Silent. `openplanet-lsp check` on the full E++ tree accepted the file.

## Workaround
`_cache.Get(pat, cached)` with a typed out-param (`uint64` via `?&out`, or `int64` via the dedicated overload then cast). Or `uint64(int64(_cache[pat]))` using the existing `int64 opConv()`.

## Acceptance
- [ ] `uint64 x = dict[key];` / `return dict[key];` where the return type is `uint64` is an error
- [ ] `int64 x = dict[key];` and `double x = dict[key];` stay silent (`int64`/`double` opConv exist)
- [ ] `dict.Get(key, uint64_out)` stays silent
- [ ] Regression fixture

## Notes
`dictionaryValue` also has `void opConv(?&out)` / `void opCast(?&out)` — those are explicit. The game rejected the implicit `uint64` path only.